{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat AGENTS.md'","aggregated_output":"# Working in this repository\n\nAxylo is a browser charting library. The product is specified in `docs/02-product-spec.md`; the build plan is `docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md`. Read the sections your task names before writing code.\n\n## Rules for every change\n\n- **Contracts are fixed.** `packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts` and `packages/axylo/src/public.ts` are the interfaces between modules. Do not edit them. If your work needs a change there, stop that part, finish what you can, and describe the exact change you need in your report.\n- **Stay in your files.** Each task lists the directories it owns. Do not create, edit or delete anything else, including configuration and other modules. Several agents work in this checkout at the same time.\n- **No runtime dependencies.** Use the platform (`Intl`, typed arrays). Dev dependencies already installed: TypeScript, Vitest, fast-check, esbuild, Playwright (system Chrome), axe-core. The network is not available; do not try to install anything.\n- **No DOM at import time.** A module that needs the DOM takes it as a parameter or touches it inside a function. Pure stages (data, scales, formatting, layout, scene) must run in Node.\n- **Hot paths use typed arrays.** No object per data point, no array of arrays per data point, no copying of large columns that the contracts say are borrowed.\n- **Never guess silently.** Anything that cannot be drawn as given is reported through the `DiagnosticSink` with the code from spec section 3.5.\n- **Tests come from the spec.** Expected values are derived from the specification and the fixture data, never by running the implementation and pasting its output. Use fast-check property tests for invariants (\"for any data …\"). A test you cannot make pass is reported as failing; do not weaken it or change its expected value.\n- **TypeScript strict, no `any`** in exported signatures. `__DEV__` is a build-time boolean (true in tests).\n- **Comments say why**, not what. Names are plain words.\n- **Do not commit.** The coordinator commits.\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\nnpm run typecheck      # tsc over the library, its tests, and the API examples in docs/api\nnpm test               # unit and property tests (Node)\nnpm run build          # packages/axylo/dist\nnpm run test:browser   # browser tests against the built bundle, in system Chrome\n```\n\n## Your report\n\nEnd with a short report: what you built (files), what you verified and how (paste the last lines of the test run), what is not done or not verified, any contract change you need, and any place where the spec was ambiguous and what you assumed. Keep \"ran and saw\" apart from \"expect\".\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat -n packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts'","aggregated_output":"     1\t/**\n     2\t * Internal contracts of Axylo. Every module is written against these types and against nothing else in\n     3\t * another module. Changing this file is an architecture change: it needs a reason recorded in the commit.\n     4\t *\n     5\t * Pipeline (docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md, section 2):\n     6\t *\n     7\t *   options ─► normalize ─► Frame ─┬─► View ─► Layout ─► Scene ─► MarkRenderer / TextLayer\n     8\t *                │ diagnostics      ├─► lookup (exact values)\n     9\t *                                   ├─► summary, table\n    10\t *                                   └─► focus model\n    11\t *\n    12\t * Rule that must never be broken: exact values, the table, keyboard navigation, tooltips, summaries and\n    13\t * events read the Frame. The Scene is geometry for drawing and may be simplified. Nothing reads values\n    14\t * back from the Scene.\n    15\t */\n    16\timport type { Diagnostic, XValue } from '../public';\n    17\t\n    18\t// ───────────────────────────── diagnostics ─────────────────────────────\n    19\t\n    20\t/**\n    21\t * What a diagnostic did to the chart. Drives the reader's note (spec F12): only 'omitted' and 'changed'\n    22\t * count towards \"N values not shown\"; a warning about contrast or an unknown option does not.\n    23\t */\n    24\texport type DiagnosticEffect = 'none' | 'omitted' | 'changed' | 'series-disabled' | 'chart-error';\n    25\t\n    26\t/** A diagnostic before the chart adds its own name. */\n    27\texport type DiagnosticInput = Omit<Diagnostic, 'chart'> & {\n    28\t  readonly effect: DiagnosticEffect;\n    29\t  /**\n    30\t   * 'call': found while validating a create, update or append call; a `strict` chart throws from that call.\n    31\t   * 'presentation': found later (a contrast check after a CSS change, a formatter that throws on a lazily\n    32\t   * built table cell, a label that no longer fits after a resize); reported when found, never thrown.\n    33\t   */\n    34\t  readonly origin: 'call' | 'presentation';\n    35\t};\n    36\t\n    37\texport interface DiagnosticSink {\n    38\t  /** Adds one diagnostic. The sink merges by code, field and effect: counts are added, example rows capped at 10. */\n    39\t  add(d: DiagnosticInput): void;\n    40\t}\n    41\t\n    42\t// ───────────────────────────── frame ─────────────────────────────\n    43\t\n    44\t/**\n    45\t * What an x value is.\n    46\t *  number   – a plain measure.\n    47\t *  time     – an instant. Position = epoch milliseconds (UTC). Shown in `XColumn.timeZone`.\n    48\t *  date     – a calendar date, month or year. Position = epoch milliseconds of that date at 00:00 UTC;\n    49\t *             always formatted in UTC, so it reads the same in every viewer zone.\n    50\t *  wall     – a date-time written without an offset. Position = the written fields read as if UTC;\n    51\t *             always formatted in UTC (\"shown as written\").\n    52\t *  category – a name. Position = index in first-seen order (bar, line) or given order (donut).\n    53\t */\n    54\texport type XKind = 'number' | 'time' | 'date' | 'wall' | 'category';\n    55\t\n    56\t/** State of one slot of an aligned series. */\n    57\texport const SLOT_VALUE = 0;         // a finite number\n    58\texport const SLOT_NULL = 1;          // explicit null (or NaN in a typed column, or an empty string): \"no data\", silent\n    59\texport const SLOT_INVALID = 2;       // present but not plottable (NaN or infinity in a row, a stray string): reported\n    60\texport const SLOT_NO_ROW = 3;        // this series has no observation at this x and none was expected; neighbours may be joined across it\n    61\texport const SLOT_GAP = 4;           // an expected step of this series is absent (AX105): never joined across\n    62\texport const SLOT_ABSENT_FIELD = 5;  // the row exists but the field's key is absent or undefined (AX102)\n    63\texport type SlotState = 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5;\n    64\t/**\n    65\t * `missing: 'zero'` on a value field is applied by normalization: slots that would be SLOT_NULL, SLOT_NO_ROW,\n    66\t * SLOT_GAP or SLOT_ABSENT_FIELD become SLOT_VALUE with y = 0 and row = -1. SLOT_INVALID is never turned into zero.\n    67\t */\n    68\t\n    69\t/** Half-open range of indexes. */\n    70\texport interface IndexRange { readonly start: number; readonly end: number }\n    71\t\n    72\texport interface XColumn {\n    73\t  readonly kind: XKind;\n    74\t  /** Strictly ascending positions, one per slot. For 'category': 0, 1, 2, … */\n    75\t  readonly values: Float64Array;\n    76\t  /** For 'category': the name of each position. Otherwise null. */\n    77\t  readonly categories: readonly string[] | null;\n    78\t  /** For 'time': the resolved IANA zone ('UTC', 'America/Los_Angeles', …; 'local' is resolved before it gets here). Otherwise null. */\n    79\t  readonly timeZone: string | null;\n    80\t  /** For 'date': the precision the values were written in ('2026-02' is a month); the finest one if they are mixed. Otherwise null. */\n    81\t  readonly dateUnit: 'day' | 'month' | 'year' | null;\n    82\t  /** For 'category': true when the author declared the categories ordered, so the axis may be thinned (spec L1). */\n    83\t  readonly ordered: boolean;\n    84\t}\n    85\t\n    86\t/** The caller's data behind a frame, for events and for the table's provenance. */\n    87\texport interface RowSource {\n    88\t  /** The caller's row at a source index (materialized on demand for typed columns), or null if it is no longer retained. */\n    89\t  rowAt(sourceIndex: number): unknown;\n    90\t}\n    91\t\n    92\t/** One series of an aligned frame: a y value and a state for every x slot. */\n    93\texport interface Series {\n    94\t  /** Stable identity: the series value (long form) or the field name (wide form). Used for colors and toggling. */\n    95\t  readonly key: string;\n    96\t  /** Name shown to the reader. */\n    97\t  readonly label: string;\n    98\t  /** The value field this series was read from, for diagnostics. */\n    99\t  readonly field: string;\n   100\t  readonly unit: string | null;\n   101\t  readonly valueScale: 'percent' | 'ratio' | null;\n   102\t  /** False when the series cannot be drawn (duplicate x, AX108). It stays in the frame so the table and summary can say so. */\n   103\t  readonly drawable: boolean;\n   104\t  /** y per slot. NaN wherever `slot` is not SLOT_VALUE. May be a view on the caller's typed column. */\n   105\t  readonly y: Float64Array | Float32Array;\n   106\t  readonly slot: Uint8Array;\n   107\t  /** Index of the caller's row each slot came from, -1 where there is none. null means \"slot i came from row i\" (typed columns). */\n   108\t  readonly row: Int32Array | null;\n   109\t}\n   110\t\n   111\t/** One series of a point frame (scatter): its own x and y, sorted by x then y. */\n   112\texport interface PointSeries {\n   113\t  readonly key: string;\n   114\t  readonly label: string;\n   115\t  readonly drawable: boolean;\n   116\t  readonly x: Float64Array;\n   117\t  readonly y: Float64Array;\n   118\t  readonly row: Int32Array | null;\n   119\t}\n   120\t\n   121\t/**\n   122\t * The normalized, lossless data. Immutable: an update or append produces a new frame with a higher revision.\n   123\t * Buffers may be shared between revisions; a streaming store appends into spare capacity and hands out\n   124\t * subarray views, so an append does not copy what is already there.\n   125\t */\n   126\tinterface FrameBase {\n   127\t  readonly revision: number;\n   128\t  /** Changes when the data is replaced or the encoding changes; survives append and eviction. A DatumRef is only meaningful within one epoch. */\n   129\t  readonly epoch: number;\n   130\t  readonly source: RowSource;\n   131\t}\n   132\t\n   133\texport interface AlignedFrame extends FrameBase {\n   134\t  readonly shape: 'aligned';\n   135\t  readonly x: XColumn;\n   136\t  readonly series: readonly Series[];\n   137\t  /** Number of x slots. */\n   138\t  readonly length: number;\n   139\t  readonly xLabel: string;\n   140\t  readonly yLabel: string | null;\n   141\t}\n   142\t\n   143\texport interface PointFrame extends FrameBase {\n   144\t  readonly shape: 'points';\n   145\t  readonly xKind: Exclude<XKind, 'category'>;\n   146\t  readonly timeZone: string | null;\n   147\t  readonly series: readonly PointSeries[];\n   148\t  readonly xLabel: string;\n   149\t  readonly yLabel: string;\n   150\t  readonly xUnit: string | null;\n   151\t  readonly yUnit: string | null;\n   152\t}\n   153\t\n   154\t/** Donut data: every category the caller gave, in the given order, before any grouping into \"Other\". */\n   155\texport interface DonutFrame extends FrameBase {\n   156\t  readonly shape: 'donut';\n   157\t  readonly labels: readonly string[];\n   158\t  /** NaN where `slot` is not SLOT_VALUE. */\n   159\t  readonly values: Float64Array;\n   160\t  readonly slot: Uint8Array;\n   161\t  readonly row: Int32Array | null;\n   162\t  readonly valueLabel: string;\n   163\t  readonly unit: string | null;\n   164\t  readonly valueScale: 'percent' | 'ratio' | null;\n   165\t}\n   166\t\n   167\texport type Frame = AlignedFrame | PointFrame | DonutFrame;\n   168\t\n   169\t/**\n   170\t * Join rule for lines and areas (spec F2). Two consecutive SLOT_VALUE slots i < j of one series are joined\n   171\t * if and only if every slot strictly between them is SLOT_NO_ROW. A value with no joined neighbour on either\n   172\t * side is an isolated point and must be drawn as a visible point.\n   173\t */\n   174\t\n   175\t// ───────────────────────────── formatting ─────────────────────────────\n   176\t\n   177\texport interface Formatters {\n   178\t  /** Value as readers see it in tooltip, table and announcements: full precision per spec F6, unit appended. */\n   179\t  value(seriesIndex: number, v: number): string;\n   180\t  /** x as readers see it in tooltip, table and announcements. For 'time' it includes the zone abbreviation. */\n   181\t  x(position: number): string;\n   182\t  /** Text for a slot that is not a value: \"No data\", \"No observation\". */\n   183\t  missing(state: SlotState): string;\n   184\t}\n   185\t\n   186\t// ───────────────────────────── scales and ticks ─────────────────────────────\n   187\t\n   188\texport interface ContinuousScale {\n   189\t  readonly type: 'linear' | 'time';\n   190\t  readonly domain: readonly [number, number];\n   191\t  /** Pixel range in CSS px; range[0] maps domain[0]. */\n   192\t  readonly range: readonly [number, number];\n   193\t  map(value: number): number;\n   194\t  invert(pixel: number): number;\n   195\t}\n   196\t\n   197\texport interface BandScale {\n   198\t  readonly type: 'band';\n   199\t  readonly count: number;\n   200\t  readonly range: readonly [number, number];\n   201\t  /** Distance between the starts of adjacent bands. */\n   202\t  readonly step: number;\n   203\t  /** Width of one band after padding. */\n   204\t  readonly bandwidth: number;\n   205\t  /** Start pixel of band i. */\n   206\t  map(index: number): number;\n   207\t  center(index: number): number;\n   208\t  /** Band under a pixel, clamped to [0, count - 1]; -1 when count is 0. */\n   209\t  invert(pixel: number): number;\n   210\t}\n   211\t\n   212\texport type XScale = ContinuousScale | BandScale;\n   213\t\n   214\texport interface Tick {\n   215\t  /** Position in the scale's domain (category: index). */\n   216\t  readonly value: number;\n   217\t  readonly label: string;\n   218\t}\n   219\t\n   220\t/**\n   221\t * Candidate tick sets for one axis, from densest to sparsest. Layout picks the densest set that fits.\n   222\t * Every set is a subset of \"nice\" positions for that axis; for a band scale the sets are every k-th category.\n   223\t */\n   224\texport type TickCandidates = readonly (readonly Tick[])[];\n   225\t\n   226\t// ───────────────────────────── view ─────────────────────────────\n   227\t\n   228\t/** A reference line (one position) or band (two) after its values were turned into axis positions. */\n   229\texport interface ResolvedReference {\n   230\t  readonly axis: 'x' | 'y';\n   231\t  readonly from: number;\n   232\t  /** Equal to `from` for a line. */\n   233\t  readonly to: number;\n   234\t  readonly label: string;\n   235\t}\n   236\t\n   237\t/** How one series is told apart without color (spec A5): a marker shape and dash patterns. */\n   238\texport interface SeriesCue {\n   239\t  readonly marker: MarkerShape;\n   240\t  readonly dash: DashStyle;\n   241\t}\n   242\t\n   243\t/**\n   244\t * Stacking (spec F10). Positive and negative values accumulate on their own sides of zero.\n   245\t * `positive[k]` is the upper boundary of the k-th stacked series' positive part, `positive[k - 1]` (or zero\n   246\t * for k = 0) its lower boundary; likewise `negative`. A component that is not SLOT_VALUE contributes zero\n   247\t * height and sets `incomplete` for that slot.\n   248\t */\n   249\texport interface StackView {\n   250\t  /** Frame series indexes in accumulation order (hidden series are left out). */\n   251\t  readonly order: readonly number[];\n   252\t  readonly positive: readonly Float64Array[];\n   253\t  readonly negative: readonly Float64Array[];\n   254\t  /** 1 where at least one visible component is missing; null when every stack is complete. */\n   255\t  readonly incomplete: Uint8Array | null;\n   256\t}\n   257\t\n   258\tinterface CartesianViewBase {\n   259\t  readonly revision: number;\n   260\t  /** Visibility per series (legend toggles). */\n   261\t  readonly visible: readonly boolean[];\n   262\t  readonly cues: readonly SeriesCue[];\n   263\t  /** Full x domain of the data (plus the author's domain), and the zoomed domain actually shown. */\n   264\t  readonly xFull: readonly [number, number];\n   265\t  readonly xDomain: readonly [number, number];\n   266\t  /** Value domain after the rules of spec F1 and F7. */\n   267\t  readonly yDomain: readonly [number, number];\n   268\t  readonly references: readonly ResolvedReference[];\n   269\t  readonly compact: boolean;\n   270\t}\n   271\t\n   272\t/** What is currently shown of an aligned frame. */\n   273\texport interface AlignedView extends CartesianViewBase {\n   274\t  readonly kind: 'line' | 'area' | 'bar';\n   275\t  readonly frame: AlignedFrame;\n   276\t  /** True only for horizontal bars. */\n   277\t  readonly horizontal: boolean;\n   278\t  /** Slots whose x lies inside xDomain. Pointer and keyboard only ever land on these. */\n   279\t  readonly visibleSlots: IndexRange;\n   280\t  /**\n   281\t   * Per series, the slot range to draw: visibleSlots widened on each side to that series' nearest value it\n   282\t   * may be joined to, so a line reaches the plot edge. Never used for picking.\n   283\t   */\n   284\t  readonly drawSlots: readonly IndexRange[];\n   285\t  readonly stack: StackView | null;\n   286\t}\n   287\t\n   288\texport interface ScatterView extends CartesianViewBase {\n   289\t  readonly kind: 'scatter';\n   290\t  readonly frame: PointFrame;\n   291\t  /** Per series, the range of its points whose x lies inside xDomain. */\n   292\t  readonly visiblePoints: readonly IndexRange[];\n   293\t}\n   294\t\n   295\t/** One drawn slice or legend entry of a donut (spec F8). */\n   296\texport interface DonutSlice {\n   297\t  readonly key: string;\n   298\t  readonly label: string;\n   299\t  /** Indexes into the donut frame: one for an ordinary slice, several for \"Other (n)\". */\n   300\t  readonly members: readonly number[];\n   301\t  /** null = \"No data\". */\n   302\t  readonly value: number | null;\n   303\t  /** Share of the total, 0–1; null when there is no value. */\n   304\t  readonly ratio: number | null;\n   305\t  /** Start and end angle in radians, clockwise from 12 o'clock; null when nothing is drawn (zero or no data). */\n   306\t  readonly angles: readonly [number, number] | null;\n   307\t}\n   308\t\n   309\texport interface DonutView {\n   310\t  readonly kind: 'donut';\n   311\t  readonly revision: number;\n   312\t  readonly frame: DonutFrame;\n   313\t  readonly slices: readonly DonutSlice[];\n   314\t  readonly total: number;\n   315\t}\n   316\t\n   317\texport type View = AlignedView | ScatterView | DonutView;\n   318\t\n   319\t// ───────────────────────────── text measurement ─────────────────────────────\n   320\t\n   321\texport interface TextStyle {\n   322\t  /** CSS font shorthand resolved from the page, e.g. \"400 12px Inter, sans-serif\". */\n   323\t  readonly font: string;\n   324\t  readonly letterSpacing: number;\n   325\t  readonly wordSpacing: number;\n   326\t  /** Line height in CSS px. */\n   327\t  readonly lineHeight: number;\n   328\t}\n   329\t\n   330\t/** Injected into layout. Browser: canvas measureText with the page's computed spacing applied. Tests: fixed metrics. */\n   331\texport interface TextMeasurer {\n   332\t  width(text: string, style: TextStyle): number;\n   333\t}\n   334\t\n   335\t// ───────────────────────────── layout ─────────────────────────────\n   336\t\n   337\texport interface Rect { readonly x: number; readonly y: number; readonly width: number; readonly height: number }\n   338\t\n   339\texport type LabelRemedy = 'thinned' | 'wrapped' | 'rotated' | 'truncated';\n   340\t\n   341\texport interface PlacedText {\n   342\t  /** What is drawn (possibly truncated with an ellipsis in the middle). */\n   343\t  readonly lines: readonly string[];\n   344\t  /** The complete text, for tooltip and table. */\n   345\t  readonly full: string;\n   346\t  /** Anchor point in CSS px relative to the plot container. */\n   347\t  readonly x: number;\n   348\t  readonly y: number;\n   349\t  readonly anchor: 'start' | 'middle' | 'end';\n   350\t  readonly baseline: 'top' | 'middle' | 'bottom';\n   351\t  /** Degrees, clockwise; 0, -45 or -90 in 1.0. */\n   352\t  readonly rotate: number;\n   353\t  readonly role: 'tick-x' | 'tick-y' | 'title-x' | 'title-y' | 'value' | 'reference' | 'message';\n   354\t  /** Bounding box after rotation, for the overlap test. */\n   355\t  readonly box: Rect;\n   356\t}\n   357\t\n   358\t/** The mapping from data to pixels that scene building and lookup must share. */\n   359\texport type Projection =\n   360\t  | { readonly kind: 'xy'; readonly x: XScale; readonly y: ContinuousScale }\n   361\t  /** Bars: `band` runs along the category axis, `value` along the other; `horizontal` swaps the screen axes. */\n   362\t  | { readonly kind: 'bands'; readonly horizontal: boolean; readonly band: XScale; readonly value: ContinuousScale }\n   363\t  | { readonly kind: 'ring'; readonly cx: number; readonly cy: number; readonly r0: number; readonly r1: number };\n   364\t\n   365\t/** What label fitting did on one axis, in the order it did it (spec L1). */\n   366\texport interface AxisLabelFit {\n   367\t  readonly remedies: readonly LabelRemedy[];\n   368\t  /** Labels that could not be shown after every remedy. More than zero means the reader gets the L1 note. */\n   369\t  readonly hidden: number;\n   370\t}\n   371\t\n   372\tinterface LayoutSize {\n   373\t  /** Size of the plot container (the element that holds marks and tick text), CSS px. */\n   374\t  readonly width: number;\n   375\t  readonly height: number;\n   376\t}\n   377\t\n   378\t/**\n   379\t * Layout of the plot container only. The title, summary, legend, controls, notes and table are ordinary\n   380\t * HTML around it and are laid out by the browser; the plot container's size is whatever is left.\n   381\t */\n   382\texport type Layout =\n   383\t  | (LayoutSize & {\n   384\t      readonly kind: 'plot';\n   385\t      /** Where marks are drawn. */\n   386\t      readonly plot: Rect;\n   387\t      readonly projection: Projection;\n   388\t      readonly xTicks: readonly Tick[];\n   389\t      readonly yTicks: readonly Tick[];\n   390\t      readonly texts: readonly PlacedText[];\n   391\t      readonly fit: { readonly x: AxisLabelFit; readonly y: AxisLabelFit };\n   392\t    })\n   393\t  /** Compact variant (spec 3.7): marks fill the container, no text. */\n   394\t  | (LayoutSize & { readonly kind: 'compact'; readonly plot: Rect; readonly projection: Projection })\n   395\t  /** The plot would be below 120 × 80 CSS px (spec L8): only the summary and the table control are shown. */\n   396\t  | (LayoutSize & { readonly kind: 'too-small' })\n   397\t  /** Loading, empty or error state (spec L7): a message instead of marks. */\n   398\t  | (LayoutSize & { readonly kind: 'message'; readonly text: PlacedText })\n   399\t  /** The container has no size yet (hidden or detached). Nothing is drawn until it gets one. */\n   400\t  | (LayoutSize & { readonly kind: 'unmeasured' });\n   401\t\n   402\t// ───────────────────────────── scene ─────────────────────────────\n   403\t\n   404\t/**\n   405\t * A color that is resolved late, so an SVG renderer can use CSS variables and a canvas renderer can look\n   406\t * the value up in the resolved theme.\n   407\t */\n   408\texport type Paint =\n   409\t  | { readonly kind: 'series'; readonly index: number }   // palette slot or the author's color for that series\n   410\t  | { readonly kind: 'token'; readonly name: 'axis' | 'grid' | 'reference' | 'muted' | 'focus' | 'background' | 'text' }\n   411\t  | { readonly kind: 'none' };\n   412\t\n   413\texport type MarkerShape = 'circle' | 'square' | 'triangle' | 'diamond' | 'cross' | 'plus' | 'triangle-down' | 'star';\n   414\t\n   415\t/** Dash pattern in normal mode and under `prefers-contrast: more` or forced colors. null = solid. */\n   416\texport interface DashStyle {\n   417\t  readonly normal: readonly number[] | null;\n   418\t  readonly contrast: readonly number[] | null;\n   419\t}\n   420\t\n   421\t/** A polyline. `xy` is x0,y0,x1,y1,… in CSS px; a NaN pair lifts the pen. */\n   422\texport interface PathMark {\n   423\t  readonly type: 'path';\n   424\t  readonly series: number;\n   425\t  readonly xy: Float32Array;\n   426\t  readonly stroke: Paint;\n   427\t  readonly strokeWidth: number;\n   428\t  readonly dash: DashStyle;\n   429\t}\n   430\t\n   431\t/**\n   432\t * Filled regions between an upper and a lower boundary (area, stacked area). Each boundary is its own packed\n   433\t * polyline, so each can keep its own extremes when simplified (spec F5), and adjacent stack bands can share\n   434\t * the very same boundary array. `runs` holds quadruples (upperStart, upperCount, lowerStart, lowerCount) in\n   435\t * vertices; one quadruple is one polygon: its upper vertices forward, then its lower vertices in reverse.\n   436\t */\n   437\texport interface AreaMark {\n   438\t  readonly type: 'area';\n   439\t  readonly series: number;\n   440\t  readonly upper: Float32Array;\n   441\t  readonly lower: Float32Array;\n   442\t  readonly runs: Uint32Array;\n   443\t  readonly fill: Paint;\n   444\t  readonly opacity: number;\n   445\t}\n   446\t\n   447\t/** Axis-aligned rectangles: x,y,width,height quadruples in CSS px. */\n   448\texport interface RectMark {\n   449\t  readonly type: 'rects';\n   450\t  readonly series: number;\n   451\t  readonly xywh: Float32Array;\n   452\t  readonly fill: Paint;\n   453\t  /** 'missing' draws the \"no data\" mark of spec F2 instead of a filled bar. */\n   454\t  readonly variant: 'bar' | 'missing';\n   455\t}\n   456\t\n   457\t/** Markers: x,y pairs in CSS px. */\n   458\texport interface PointMark {\n   459\t  readonly type: 'points';\n   460\t  readonly series: number;\n   461\t  readonly xy: Float32Array;\n   462\t  readonly shape: MarkerShape;\n   463\t  readonly size: number;\n   464\t  readonly fill: Paint;\n   465\t}\n   466\t\n   467\t/** Annular sectors (donut). Angles in radians, clockwise from 12 o'clock. */\n   468\texport interface ArcMark {\n   469\t  readonly type: 'arcs';\n   470\t  readonly cx: number;\n   471\t  readonly cy: number;\n   472\t  readonly r0: number;\n   473\t  readonly r1: number;\n   474\t  readonly angles: Float32Array; // start0,end0,start1,end1,…\n   475\t  readonly fills: readonly Paint[];\n   476\t  /** Gap between adjacent slices in CSS px (spec A5). */\n   477\t  readonly gap: number;\n   478\t}\n   479\t\n   480\texport interface RuleMark {\n   481\t  readonly type: 'rule';\n   482\t  readonly x1: number; readonly y1: number; readonly x2: number; readonly y2: number;\n   483\t  readonly stroke: Paint;\n   484\t  readonly strokeWidth: number;\n   485\t  readonly dash: readonly number[] | null;\n   486\t  readonly role: 'grid' | 'axis' | 'tick' | 'reference' | 'cursor' | 'break';\n   487\t}\n   488\t\n   489\t/** A filled rectangle that is not data: a reference band. */\n   490\texport interface BandMark {\n   491\t  readonly type: 'band';\n   492\t  readonly box: Rect;\n   493\t  readonly fill: Paint;\n   494\t  readonly opacity: number;\n   495\t}\n   496\t\n   497\texport type Mark = PathMark | AreaMark | RectMark | PointMark | ArcMark | RuleMark | BandMark;\n   498\t\n   499\t/** Everything the mark renderer draws, back to front. Plain data: no functions, no DOM. */\n   500\texport interface Scene {\n   501\t  readonly width: number;\n   502\t  readonly height: number;\n   503\t  /** Marks are clipped to this rectangle unless their role is 'axis' or 'tick'. */\n   504\t  readonly clip: Rect;\n   505\t  readonly marks: readonly Mark[];\n   506\t}\n   507\t\n   508\t// ───────────────────────────── theme ─────────────────────────────\n   509\t\n   510\texport type PaintToken = 'axis' | 'grid' | 'reference' | 'muted' | 'focus' | 'background' | 'text';\n   511\t\n   512\t/** CSS color expressions per paint. May be `var(--axylo-series-1)` or an author's `var(--brand-1)`: unresolved. */\n   513\texport interface PaintBindings {\n   514\t  readonly tokens: Readonly<Record<PaintToken, string>>;\n   515\t  /** One expression per series index, already including the author's `colors` by series key. */\n   516\t  readonly series: readonly string[];\n   517\t}\n   518\t\n   519\t/** The same paints as concrete computed colors, plus what was detected about the page (spec L4, DX6). */\n   520\texport interface ResolvedTheme {\n   521\t  readonly scheme: 'light' | 'dark';\n   522\t  readonly forcedColors: boolean;\n   523\t  readonly moreContrast: boolean;\n   524\t  readonly paints: PaintBindings;\n   525\t}\n   526\t\n   527\t// ───────────────────────────── rendering ─────────────────────────────\n   528\t\n   529\t/** Transient decoration drawn above the scene: cursor rule and highlighted points (clipped to the plot), focus ring (not clipped). */\n   530\texport interface Overlay {\n   531\t  readonly clip: Rect;\n   532\t  readonly clipped: readonly Mark[];\n   533\t  readonly unclipped: readonly Mark[];\n   534\t}\n   535\t\n   536\t/**\n   537\t * Draws a scene's marks. Two implementations exist for the M1 comparison (canvas, svg); the rest of the\n   538\t * library does not know which one is in use.\n   539\t *\n   540\t * A canvas renderer paints with `theme.paints` (concrete colors) and must be told to draw again when the\n   541\t * theme changes. An SVG renderer paints with `bindings` (CSS expressions), so the browser restyles it on a\n   542\t * theme change without a call; it switches dash patterns with CSS media queries.\n   543\t */\n   544\texport interface MarkRenderer {\n   545\t  readonly kind: 'canvas' | 'svg';\n   546\t  /** The element to insert into the plot container. It must be aria-hidden. */\n   547\t  readonly element: HTMLElement | SVGSVGElement;\n   548\t  /** Draws the scene, replacing the previous one. Called at most once per animation frame. */\n   549\t  draw(scene: Scene, bindings: PaintBindings, theme: ResolvedTheme, devicePixelRatio: number): void;\n   550\t  /** Draws or clears (null) the overlay without redrawing the scene. */\n   551\t  drawOverlay(overlay: Overlay | null, bindings: PaintBindings, theme: ResolvedTheme, devicePixelRatio: number): void;\n   552\t  destroy(): void;\n   553\t}\n   554\t\n   555\t// ───────────────────────────── lookup ─────────────────────────────\n   556\t\n   557\t/**\n   558\t * A datum by identity, not by position, so it still means the same thing after a streaming window slides.\n   559\t * Valid within one frame epoch.\n   560\t */\n   561\texport type DatumRef =\n   562\t  | { readonly kind: 'aligned'; readonly seriesKey: string; /** x position (category: its index at the time; categories do not slide). */ readonly x: number }\n   563\t  | { readonly kind: 'point'; readonly seriesKey: string; /** source row index */ readonly row: number }\n   564\t  | { readonly kind: 'slice'; readonly sliceKey: string };\n   565\t\n   566\t/** What the pointer is over, by the picking rule of the chart type (spec 3.6). */\n   567\texport type PickTarget =\n   568\t  | { readonly kind: 'x'; readonly x: number }                      // line, area, bar: every series at this x\n   569\t  | { readonly kind: 'point'; readonly refs: readonly DatumRef[]; readonly count: number }  // scatter: nearest point and those coinciding with it (at most 8; `count` is the full number)\n   570\t  | { readonly kind: 'slice'; readonly sliceKey: string };\n   571\t\n   572\t/** One row of a tooltip or one announced point, as text. All text comes from the frame through the formatters. */\n   573\texport interface DatumText {\n   574\t  readonly ref: DatumRef;\n   575\t  readonly seriesIndex: number;\n   576\t  readonly seriesLabel: string;\n   577\t  /** x as the reader sees it. */\n   578\t  readonly x: string;\n   579\t  /** The value with its unit, or \"No data\" / \"No observation\". */\n   580\t  readonly value: string;\n   581\t  readonly state: SlotState;\n   582\t  /** Share of the whole for a donut slice, formatted; null elsewhere. */\n   583\t  readonly percent: string | null;\n   584\t  /** Source row index, or -1. */\n   585\t  readonly row: number;\n   586\t}\n   587\t\n   588\texport interface TooltipModel {\n   589\t  /** Heading: the x value (with its time zone for instants), the category, or the slice label. */\n   590\t  readonly title: string;\n   591\t  /** At most eight rows (spec I1). */\n   592\t  readonly rows: readonly DatumText[];\n   593\t  /** Rows before truncation. */\n   594\t  readonly count: number;\n   595\t  /** Stack total with \"incomplete\" where it applies, already formatted; null when the chart does not stack. */\n   596\t  readonly total: string | null;\n   597\t}\n   598\t\n   599\texport type StepDirection = 'next' | 'previous' | 'first' | 'last' | 'series-next' | 'series-previous' | 'page-next' | 'page-previous';\n   600\t\n   601\t/**\n   602\t * Exact answers from the frame for one view and projection, independent of how the scene was simplified.\n   603\t * Built once per (view, layout); cheap to build: binary search over x for aligned frames, a grid index for scatter.\n   604\t */\n   605\texport interface Lookup {\n   606\t  /** What is under a pixel of the plot container, or null. */\n   607\t  pick(px: number, py: number): PickTarget | null;\n   608\t  tooltip(target: PickTarget): TooltipModel;\n   609\t  /** The datum to focus when the keyboard takes over from a pointer target. */\n   610\t  primary(target: PickTarget): DatumRef | null;\n   611\t  datum(ref: DatumRef): DatumText | null;\n   612\t  /** Where the datum is drawn, for the cursor and focus ring; null if it is not visible. */\n   613\t  anchor(ref: DatumRef): Rect | null;\n   614\t  /** Number of data the keyboard can reach in the current view, and a datum's place among them (zero based, -1 if absent). */\n   615\t  readonly count: number;\n   616\t  ordinal(ref: DatumRef): number;\n   617\t  /** Keyboard order per chart type (spec 3.6). `from` null starts at the first datum. Skips hidden series. */\n   618\t  step(from: DatumRef | null, direction: StepDirection): DatumRef | null;\n   619\t  /** After the data moved on: the same datum if it is still there, else the next one that is, else the previous, else null. */\n   620\t  resolve(ref: DatumRef): DatumRef | null;\n   621\t}\n   622\t\n   623\t// ───────────────────────────── reader model ─────────────────────────────\n   624\t\n   625\t/** The table of spec A4, built lazily from the frame: nothing is materialized until a page is asked for. */\n   626\texport interface TableModel {\n   627\t  readonly caption: string;\n   628\t  /** First entry is the x column. */\n   629\t  readonly headers: readonly string[];\n   630\t  readonly rowCount: number;\n   631\t  readonly pageSize: number;\n   632\t  /** Cells of one row as text; first cell is the row header. null outside the range. */\n   633\t  row(ordinal: number): readonly string[] | null;\n   634\t  /** Zero-based page that contains the first row at or after an x value; null if there is none. */\n   635\t  pageForX(x: XValue): number | null;\n   636\t}\n   637\t\n   638\t/** Everything a reader gets as text (spec A1, C1). */\n   639\texport interface ReaderModel {\n   640\t  /** Accessible name: the title, or a generated one. Empty when the chart is named by `labelledBy`. */\n   641\t  readonly name: string;\n   642\t  /** Generated summary plus the author's description, including time zone and omission statements. */\n   643\t  readonly summary: string;\n   644\t  /** The reader's note of spec F12 and L1, or null. */\n   645\t  readonly note: string | null;\n   646\t  /** null for the compact variant and when the table is turned off. */\n   647\t  readonly table: TableModel | null;\n   648\t}\n   649\t\n   650\t// ───────────────────────────── environment ─────────────────────────────\n   651\t\n   652\t/** Everything outside the options and data that output depends on. Part of every cache key that needs it. */\n   653\texport interface Environment {\n   654\t  readonly locale: string;\n   655\t  /** The viewer's zone, used when a time field says 'local'. */\n   656\t  readonly timeZone: string;\n   657\t  readonly devicePixelRatio: number;\n   658\t  readonly reducedMotion: boolean;\n   659\t  readonly textStyle: TextStyle;\n   660\t  /** Increases whenever web fonts finish loading; part of the layout cache key. */\n   661\t  readonly fontEpoch: number;\n   662\t  readonly development: boolean;\n   663\t}\n   664\t\n   665\texport type { Diagnostic, XValue };\n   666\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
