{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'L2|L4|A5|A6|DX6|DX8|C4|F2|\"'^#{1,5} 2'\"\\\\.[34]|\"'^#{1,5} 2'\"\\\\.5' docs/02-product-spec.md docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md\"","aggregated_output":"docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:86:| `missing` (value) | `'gap'` (default) or `'zero'` (F2). |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:101:| `colors` | A fixed color per series name (DX6). |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:200:| mark raster | Scene; device pixel ratio; resolved colors (L4's triggers). |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:204:### 2.3 Rendering\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:206:**Working assumption: Canvas 2D for marks, HTML for all text.** Text stays in the DOM so that it inherits the page font and color, honors user text spacing and zoom (A6), adapts in forced-colors mode, and can be selected and translated.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:216:### 2.4 Document structure\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:239:### 2.5 Repository\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:286:- The diagnostic registry (F3, F12); missing values and absent steps (F2); the three temporal types (F4); formatting (F6); domains (F7); sorting and duplicates (F11); `validate()`.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:311:- The pattern chosen in M1, built fully: names and summary (A1), keyboard (A2), point text (A3), table with paging (A4), non-color cues (A5), reflow (A6), streaming behavior (A7), messages and language (A10); single-pointer zoom controls (I3, I4); reduced motion on update (I5).\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:354:- Node import and `validate()` without a DOM; SSR hydration; strict CSP with real headers (DX8).\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:375:| Property | fast-check | Invariants that must hold for any data: F1, F2, F5, F7, F11, L1. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:381:| Packed distribution | Clean install fixtures | What users actually get (DX1, DX7, DX8, DX10). |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:391:| DOM text costs too much with many charts on a page. | P5 is measured in M1. A fallback to canvas-drawn tick labels would give up user text spacing and forced-colors adaptation for those labels, so it must pass the same L1 and A6 tests before it is allowed. |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:76:### 2.3 Supported environments\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:95:| F2 | Missing values are never drawn as zero and never bridged unless the author asks. An explicit `null` is a gap, silently. An isolated value between two gaps is a visible point. A missing bar shows a \"no data\" mark at the baseline, distinct from a zero bar. On a time or date axis with a regular step, an absent step is a gap and raises AX105; `missing: 'zero'` on the field turns absent and null values into zeros for counts. Tooltip, table and announcements say \"No data\". | `trend` with nulls and `trend` with the same 7 rows deleted render the same gap; `dirty` fixtures; property test that no segment connects across a missing index | R5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:112:| L2 | Text is at least 12 CSS px and at least 4.5:1 against what is behind it, including text drawn inside a mark and legend entries for hidden series. Marks, axis lines and focus indicators are at least 3:1. Gridlines are exempt: they are not needed to read a value while the tooltip and table exist. Holds in light and dark. | Computed-style and rendered-pixel checks in both schemes | R7, R10 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:114:| L4 | Light or dark is taken from the chart element's computed `color-scheme`; if that is not set, from the luminance of the inherited text color. `--axylo-background` overrides both. Marks repaint within one frame when the scheme, forced colors, contrast preference, or the `class`, `style` or `data-theme` of `<html>` or `<body>` changes. Forced-colors mode uses system colors. | A page that sets `color-scheme`; a class-toggled dark theme without it; a light-only page on a dark device (must stay light); a runtime toggle; forced-colors emulation | R10 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:141:| A5 | Series are never distinguished by color alone, in any mode. Each line and area carries a shape marker at its last point and at sparse intervals, repeated in the legend and tooltip; under `prefers-contrast: more` or forced colors, lines also differ by dash. Adjacent filled marks (slices, stacked segments) are separated by at least 1 px of background. The default palette has eight colors, each at least 3:1 on the default light and dark backgrounds, with a minimum pairwise OKLab difference of 0.10 (provisional) under normal vision and simulated protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia. On any other background, Axylo measures the palette against the resolved background and raises AX141 below 3:1. | Palette script scoring the rendered marks of an eight-series chart in both schemes, repeats included; rendered-pixel checks of separators; a grayscale screenshot in which three crossing lines can be told apart by marker | R7, WCAG 1.4.1, 1.4.11 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:142:| A6 | Content reflows at 320 CSS px and 400% zoom without two-dimensional scrolling. User text-spacing overrides do not clip text. | Viewport and style-override tests in three engines | WCAG 1.4.10, 1.4.12 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:204:| C2 | The fidelity rules still hold: zero baseline for bar and area (F1), gaps (F2), diagnostics (F3), simplified drawing (F5), sorting (F11), no motion (I5), scheme from the page (L4). | The same fixtures as the full charts |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:206:| C4 | With more than one series, lines differ by dash as well as color, since there is no legend; AX131 suggests one series per compact chart. | Two-series fixture |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:224:| DX6 | Colors, font and spacing are CSS custom properties with documented names; the chart inherits `font-family` and `color`. `colors` pins a color to a series name so the same series has the same color on every chart. There is no theme object and no positional palette option. | Theming tests, including a 24-tile page where series subsets differ | R10 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:226:| DX8 | Importing in Node without a DOM does not throw, and `validate()` runs there. Works under React StrictMode, including setup, cleanup and setup again. Works under a Content Security Policy without `unsafe-inline` or `unsafe-eval`, served with real headers. Labels and formatter output are inserted as text, never as HTML. A target that matches no element throws an error that names the selector. | CI tests | D1 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:295:| Is the palette that meets A5 one people want to look at? | Hand-tune from the search output with the thresholds in CI. | M5. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
