{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '319,463p' packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts; sed -n '190,242p' docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md\"","aggregated_output":"// ───────────────────────────── text measurement ─────────────────────────────\n\nexport interface TextStyle {\n  /** CSS font shorthand resolved from the page, e.g. \"400 12px Inter, sans-serif\". */\n  readonly font: string;\n  readonly letterSpacing: number;\n  readonly wordSpacing: number;\n  /** Line height in CSS px. */\n  readonly lineHeight: number;\n}\n\n/** Injected into layout. Browser: canvas measureText with the page's computed spacing applied. Tests: fixed metrics. */\nexport interface TextMeasurer {\n  width(text: string, style: TextStyle): number;\n}\n\n// ───────────────────────────── layout ─────────────────────────────\n\nexport interface Rect { readonly x: number; readonly y: number; readonly width: number; readonly height: number }\n\nexport type LabelRemedy = 'thinned' | 'wrapped' | 'rotated' | 'truncated';\n\nexport interface PlacedText {\n  /** What is drawn (possibly truncated with an ellipsis in the middle). */\n  readonly lines: readonly string[];\n  /** The complete text, for tooltip and table. */\n  readonly full: string;\n  /** Anchor point in CSS px relative to the plot container. */\n  readonly x: number;\n  readonly y: number;\n  readonly anchor: 'start' | 'middle' | 'end';\n  readonly baseline: 'top' | 'middle' | 'bottom';\n  /** Degrees, clockwise; 0, -45 or -90 in 1.0. */\n  readonly rotate: number;\n  readonly role: 'tick-x' | 'tick-y' | 'title-x' | 'title-y' | 'value' | 'reference' | 'message';\n  /** Bounding box after rotation, for the overlap test. */\n  readonly box: Rect;\n}\n\n/** The mapping from data to pixels that scene building and lookup must share. */\nexport type Projection =\n  | { readonly kind: 'xy'; readonly x: XScale; readonly y: ContinuousScale }\n  /** Bars: `band` runs along the category axis, `value` along the other; `horizontal` swaps the screen axes. */\n  | { readonly kind: 'bands'; readonly horizontal: boolean; readonly band: XScale; readonly value: ContinuousScale }\n  | { readonly kind: 'ring'; readonly cx: number; readonly cy: number; readonly r0: number; readonly r1: number };\n\n/** What label fitting did on one axis, in the order it did it (spec L1). */\nexport interface AxisLabelFit {\n  readonly remedies: readonly LabelRemedy[];\n  /** Labels that could not be shown after every remedy. More than zero means the reader gets the L1 note. */\n  readonly hidden: number;\n}\n\ninterface LayoutSize {\n  /** Size of the plot container (the element that holds marks and tick text), CSS px. */\n  readonly width: number;\n  readonly height: number;\n}\n\n/**\n * Layout of the plot container only. The title, summary, legend, controls, notes and table are ordinary\n * HTML around it and are laid out by the browser; the plot container's size is whatever is left.\n */\nexport type Layout =\n  | (LayoutSize & {\n      readonly kind: 'plot';\n      /** Where marks are drawn. */\n      readonly plot: Rect;\n      readonly projection: Projection;\n      readonly xTicks: readonly Tick[];\n      readonly yTicks: readonly Tick[];\n      readonly texts: readonly PlacedText[];\n      readonly fit: { readonly x: AxisLabelFit; readonly y: AxisLabelFit };\n    })\n  /** Compact variant (spec 3.7): marks fill the container, no text. */\n  | (LayoutSize & { readonly kind: 'compact'; readonly plot: Rect; readonly projection: Projection })\n  /** The plot would be below 120 × 80 CSS px (spec L8): only the summary and the table control are shown. */\n  | (LayoutSize & { readonly kind: 'too-small' })\n  /** Loading, empty or error state (spec L7): a message instead of marks. */\n  | (LayoutSize & { readonly kind: 'message'; readonly text: PlacedText })\n  /** The container has no size yet (hidden or detached). Nothing is drawn until it gets one. */\n  | (LayoutSize & { readonly kind: 'unmeasured' });\n\n// ───────────────────────────── scene ─────────────────────────────\n\n/**\n * A color that is resolved late, so an SVG renderer can use CSS variables and a canvas renderer can look\n * the value up in the resolved theme.\n */\nexport type Paint =\n  | { readonly kind: 'series'; readonly index: number }   // palette slot or the author's color for that series\n  | { readonly kind: 'token'; readonly name: 'axis' | 'grid' | 'reference' | 'muted' | 'focus' | 'background' | 'text' }\n  | { readonly kind: 'none' };\n\nexport type MarkerShape = 'circle' | 'square' | 'triangle' | 'diamond' | 'cross' | 'plus' | 'triangle-down' | 'star';\n\n/** Dash pattern in normal mode and under `prefers-contrast: more` or forced colors. null = solid. */\nexport interface DashStyle {\n  readonly normal: readonly number[] | null;\n  readonly contrast: readonly number[] | null;\n}\n\n/** A polyline. `xy` is x0,y0,x1,y1,… in CSS px; a NaN pair lifts the pen. */\nexport interface PathMark {\n  readonly type: 'path';\n  readonly series: number;\n  readonly xy: Float32Array;\n  readonly stroke: Paint;\n  readonly strokeWidth: number;\n  readonly dash: DashStyle;\n}\n\n/**\n * Filled regions between an upper and a lower boundary (area, stacked area). Each boundary is its own packed\n * polyline, so each can keep its own extremes when simplified (spec F5), and adjacent stack bands can share\n * the very same boundary array. `runs` holds quadruples (upperStart, upperCount, lowerStart, lowerCount) in\n * vertices; one quadruple is one polygon: its upper vertices forward, then its lower vertices in reverse.\n */\nexport interface AreaMark {\n  readonly type: 'area';\n  readonly series: number;\n  readonly upper: Float32Array;\n  readonly lower: Float32Array;\n  readonly runs: Uint32Array;\n  readonly fill: Paint;\n  readonly opacity: number;\n}\n\n/** Axis-aligned rectangles: x,y,width,height quadruples in CSS px. */\nexport interface RectMark {\n  readonly type: 'rects';\n  readonly series: number;\n  readonly xywh: Float32Array;\n  readonly fill: Paint;\n  /** 'missing' draws the \"no data\" mark of spec F2 instead of a filled bar. */\n  readonly variant: 'bar' | 'missing';\n}\n\n/** Markers: x,y pairs in CSS px. */\nexport interface PointMark {\n  readonly type: 'points';\n  readonly series: number;\n  readonly xy: Float32Array;\n  readonly shape: MarkerShape;\n  readonly size: number;\n### 2.2 Invalidation\n\nStages are cached, and the cache keys are explicit. Caching on object identity alone, as the first draft said, would miss font loads, pixel-ratio changes and in-place mutation.\n\n| Stage | Reruns when |\n|---|---|\n| normalize | Data revision or field encoding changes. `append` extends the frame without renormalizing earlier rows. |\n| view model | Frame revision, zoom, series visibility, author domains. |\n| layout | View model; container size; resolved font and text spacing; `document.fonts` finishing a load; locale; any label text. A data-only update reruns layout when the tick labels would change, and skips it otherwise. |\n| scene | Layout or view model. |\n| mark raster | Scene; device pixel ratio; resolved colors (L4's triggers). |\n\nText is measured with the page's computed font, letter spacing and word spacing applied to the measuring context, and layout reruns when fonts finish loading. The measurement interface is a parameter, so Node tests inject fixed metrics and browser tests use the real one.\n\n### 2.3 Rendering\n\n**Working assumption: Canvas 2D for marks, HTML for all text.** Text stays in the DOM so that it inherits the page font and color, honors user text spacing and zoom (A6), adapts in forced-colors mode, and can be selected and translated.\n\n**This is reopened and decided in M1 by measurement.** The first draft justified canvas by Phase 1's slow SVG libraries, but those create a node per point; the one-path-per-series SVG chart in the harness was fast. With drawing simplified to a few vertices per pixel column (F5), an SVG path per series is small. SVG follows CSS variables and class-toggled themes with no repaint code, adapts to forced colors, prints sharply, needs no pixel-ratio handling and allocates no backing store (a 1,920×1,080 canvas at pixel ratio 2 is about 33 MB). Canvas is likely cheaper for per-frame redraw when streaming and hovering.\n\nM1 builds both mark renderers behind the same scene and compares them on: P1, P2, P3, P5, bytes, memory, a runtime theme toggle, forced colors, print, and browser zoom. The scene is renderer-neutral either way, so the choice is contained.\n\n**Simplified drawing.** Per device-pixel column and per contiguous run of valid samples, the stroke covers the run's minimum and maximum (F5). One rule for when it applies: more than four visible samples per device-pixel column on average. The pass over visible samples is O(visible) on typed columns and is measured separately from drawing; the vertex count is bounded by width times the number of runs, not by width alone.\n\n**No animation system.** First render is not animated (I5). Updates cut, or tween for at most 200 ms where the cost is negligible, and not at all under reduced motion.\n\n### 2.4 Document structure\n\n```html\n<figure class=\"axylo\" id=\"ax7\" role=\"group\" aria-labelledby=\"ax7-t\" aria-describedby=\"ax7-s\">\n  <figcaption>\n    <h3 id=\"ax7-t\">Daily sessions by channel</h3>        <!-- level from options; or omitted when labelledBy is used -->\n    <p id=\"ax7-s\" class=\"axylo-summary\">Line chart, 3 series, …</p>\n  </figcaption>\n  <div class=\"axylo-plot\" tabindex=\"0\"> … marks … <div class=\"axylo-text\" aria-hidden=\"true\">tick labels</div></div>\n  <div class=\"axylo-toolbar\" role=\"toolbar\" aria-label=\"Chart controls\">   <!-- one tab stop, roving focus -->\n    legend toggles · zoom in · zoom out · reset · pause · view as table\n  </div>\n  <p class=\"axylo-note\" role=\"status\">2 values not shown. See table.</p>\n  <div class=\"axylo-live\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div>\n  <div class=\"axylo-tooltip\" hidden></div>\n  <div class=\"axylo-table\" hidden><!-- built when opened: caption, headers, pager --></div>\n</figure>\n```\n\nIds are generated per chart. The plot's role, and how a focused point is conveyed, are not fixed here: M1 runs a spike with three candidate patterns and M4 confirms the choice (section 4).\n\nDefault styles are applied without injecting a `<style>` element, and a standalone stylesheet ships for pages that prefer to load it themselves. Which mechanism passes a strict Content Security Policy is settled by the M7 test with real headers, not assumed.\n\n### 2.5 Repository\n\n```\npackages/axylo/        core library (src/, test/)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
