{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'axylo[-.]css|--axylo-[a-z-]*(font|space)|styles|font|axylo-plot' docs packages/axylo/package.json scripts -g '\"'!*.json'\"' | head -n 125; rg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' packages\"","aggregated_output":"packages/axylo/package.json:15:    \"./axylo.css\": \"./dist/axylo.css\"\nscripts/build.mjs:14:if (fs.existsSync(`${pkg}/src/axylo.css`)) fs.copyFileSync(`${pkg}/src/axylo.css`, `${pkg}/dist/axylo.css`);\nscripts/size.mjs:7:const css = fs.existsSync(`${pkg}/dist/axylo.css`) ? gzipSync(fs.readFileSync(`${pkg}/dist/axylo.css`)).length : 0;\ndocs/04-plan-performance.md:104:3. **State a hypothesis that can fail,** with a number: \"Layout takes 41% of W-page because every tick label is measured twice; caching by font and string will cut W-page by at least 25%.\"\ndocs/01-landscape.md:139:- No task customizes anything: no brand colors, fonts or formatters. The brief asked how developers customize charts; that part of the comparison was not done.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:192:Stages are cached, and the cache keys are explicit. Caching on object identity alone, as the first draft said, would miss font loads, pixel-ratio changes and in-place mutation.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:198:| layout | View model; container size; resolved font and text spacing; `document.fonts` finishing a load; locale; any label text. A data-only update reruns layout when the tick labels would change, and skips it otherwise. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:202:Text is measured with the page's computed font, letter spacing and word spacing applied to the measuring context, and layout reruns when fonts finish loading. The measurement interface is a parameter, so Node tests inject fixed metrics and browser tests use the real one.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:206:**Working assumption: Canvas 2D for marks, HTML for all text.** Text stays in the DOM so that it inherits the page font and color, honors user text spacing and zoom (A6), adapts in forced-colors mode, and can be selected and translated.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:224:  <div class=\"axylo-plot\" tabindex=\"0\"> … marks … <div class=\"axylo-text\" aria-hidden=\"true\">tick labels</div></div>\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:237:Default styles are applied without injecting a `<style>` element, and a standalone stylesheet ships for pages that prefer to load it themselves. Which mechanism passes a strict Content Security Policy is settled by the M7 test with real headers, not assumed.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:302:- L1's property test in three engines, including text-spacing overrides and a late-loading font, on a category-axis line chart with long labels.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:377:| Browser | Playwright on three engines | Real text boxes, resize, pointer, touch, keyboard, time zones, color schemes, reduced motion, fonts loading late. |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:111:| L1 | No visible text overlaps other text or is clipped, and no label disappears without the reader being told. Remedies, in order: thin (time, date, numeric and `ordered` category axes only); wrap to two lines; rotate up to 45°; truncate in the middle, keeping every label distinct, with the full text in tooltip and table. If labels still do not fit, a visible note (\"Some labels hidden. See table.\") appears and AX143 suggests horizontal bars. Axylo never changes a chart's orientation on its own. | In real browsers, after fonts load: for widths 240–1,920 px and generated label sets, zero intersecting text boxes (1 px tolerance), zero text outside the figure, truncated labels pairwise distinct. Repeated with the WCAG 1.4.12 text-spacing overrides, 200% text-only zoom, and a font that loads late | R2 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:128:| I5 | First render is not animated. An update may transition for at most 200 ms. Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` nothing transitions, on first render or on update. | After `document.fonts.ready`: first frame equals the frame at 2.5 s within a 0.1% pixel tolerance, in both settings; an update under reduced motion reaches its final frame in one step; a 24-chart filter change settles within 200 ms | R14 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:224:| DX6 | Colors, font and spacing are CSS custom properties with documented names; the chart inherits `font-family` and `color`. `colors` pins a color to a series name so the same series has the same color on every chart. There is no theme object and no positional palette option. | Theming tests, including a 24-tile page where series subsets differ | R10 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:270:| Colors and fonts from CSS | R10. | Kept. Repaint triggers specified; `palette` option replaced by `colors` keyed by series name. |\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
