{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"agent_message","text":"Two defects block release. Both renderers can draw a dominant donut slice outside its outer radius, and both can erase the missing-value mark on an all-negative bar chart.\n\nI reviewed the requested source, tests, contracts, and spec sections read-only. **Ran** below means an in-memory Node experiment against repository code. **Reasoned** means I traced the implementation without observing browser pixels. I changed no files and ran neither Vitest nor a browser. None of the proposed fixes requires changing the fixed contracts.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **B · Ran — A nearly full slice loses its hole and can extend beyond the donut.** With `r0=25`, `r1=40`, `gap=1`, and a 99.9% slice, `sector` returned an apex **159.16 px** from the center. Both renderers draw to that apex. A full turn starting at `0.3` radians, stored in the contract’s `Float32Array`, missed the full-ring tolerance and produced an apex over eight million pixels away. `ArcMark` requires an annular sector, and A5 requires a constant-width separator. Determine whether the inner arc survives from its remaining angular span, handle reflex sectors explicitly, and recognize full turns at the precision of the input. The current property test stops below π and accepts any `SECTOR_NONE` result. [geometry.ts:81](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/geometry.ts:81) · [geometry.test.ts:33](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/render/geometry.test.ts:33)\n\n2. **B · Ran geometry, reasoned clipping — Missing bars disappear when zero is at the top or right.** For a vertical slot `(10,20,20,0)` on a plot starting at `y=20`, the entire missing marker occupies `y=14…20`. For a horizontal slot at the right edge `x=380`, it occupies `x=380…386`. The required plot clip removes the ink in both cases, so missing and zero look identical, violating F2. Grow the marker toward the plot interior and constrain its category extent so a narrow slot cannot cover its neighbor. Test both orientations with all-negative data. [geometry.ts:55](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/geometry.ts:55) · [canvas.ts:213](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/canvas.ts:213) · [svg.ts:139](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/svg.ts:139)\n\n3. **M · Reasoned — The contrast check can measure a background that is never painted.** On a black panel, set `--axylo-background: white` and pin a series to black. Resolution measures black against white, but the default sheet defines only a token. The scene canvas clears to transparent and the SVG has no background fill. The series can disappear despite a nominal 21:1 result. L2 and A5 concern the pixels behind the marks. Paint the resolved background on the plot, or measure the actual backdrop if the plot is intended to be transparent. Add a pixel test where the panel and token disagree. [css.ts:46](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:46) · [resolve.ts:25](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/resolve.ts:25) · [canvas.ts:53](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/canvas.ts:53)\n\n4. **M · Reasoned — Canvas CSS sizing is skipped when the backing dimensions already match.** A first draw at **150 × 75 CSS px, DPR 2** needs the default 300 × 150 backing store. `fit` returns before setting the CSS dimensions, so both canvases display at 300 × 150 CSS px. A fractional resize that rounds to the same backing dimensions likewise retains the old CSS size. Update CSS and backing dimensions independently, assign only changed backing dimensions, and derive the drawing transform from the actual backing-to-CSS ratios. [canvas.ts:41](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/canvas.ts:41)\n\n5. **M · Reasoned, byte count calculated — Canvas has no backing-store limit.** The requested 4,000 × 2,000 chart at DPR 3 sizes **two 12,000 × 6,000 canvases**, even with no overlay. Two materialized RGBA stores alone require **576,000,000 bytes**, about 549 MiB. A device that cannot supply the dimensions or memory can lose the chart. Plan §2.3 explicitly includes renderer memory in the comparison. Bound the effective ratio by dimension and pixel budgets, use it consistently for snapping and both layers, and allocate the overlay backing store on first use. I did not measure browser allocation or establish an engine-specific limit. [canvas.ts:41](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/canvas.ts:41) · [canvas.ts:78](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/canvas.ts:78)\n\n6. **M · Reasoned — SVG can permanently lose a pinned series color after forced colors ends.** Mount an SVG in forced colors with `Direct` pinned to a brand color. The installed stroke is `var(--axylo-series-1)`. Leaving forced colors computes a new binding, but the existing SVG still references the palette slot and shows its ordinary palette color. This breaks DX6 and the `MarkRenderer` promise of live SVG restyling. Give the series a stable CSS binding whose value switches under the media query. Test entry and exit on the **same mounted chart**, including its overlay. [resolve.ts:49](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/resolve.ts:49) · [svg.ts:315](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/svg.ts:315) · [theme.browser.test.ts:164](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/render/theme.browser.test.ts:164)\n\n7. **M · Reasoned — `color-scheme: light dark` incorrectly delegates the decision to text color.** On a dark-preference device, a chart permitting both schemes but explicitly inheriting `color: #111` is classified as light. L4 gives a declared scheme precedence over text luminance. I interpret a list as selecting the browser’s used scheme from the permitted schemes. Resolve that choice in the chart’s context, and reserve the text fallback for an unset or `normal` scheme. The existing test uses default text whose color already follows the device, so either algorithm passes. [resolve.ts:78](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/resolve.ts:78) · [theme.browser.test.ts:63](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/render/theme.browser.test.ts:63)\n\n8. **M · Reasoned — A chart-local theme change can leave marks stale indefinitely.** Toggle `data-theme` on a card between `<body>` and the chart. Initial resolution reads the chart’s inherited style correctly, but the watcher only observes `<html>` and the body present at setup. Canvas keeps its pixels, and SVG can retain its old `data-axylo-scheme`. Replacing an existing body also leaves the observer on the old body. L4 requires a repaint within one frame of a scheme change. Observe the chart and relevant ancestors, rebind on reparenting or body replacement, and cover stylesheet-driven changes that alter the computed scheme. [watch.ts:29](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/watch.ts:29)\n\n9. **M · Ran — Alpha can suppress AX141 for an invisible series.** For black ink and `rgba(0,0,0,0.1)` over a black panel, the actual contrast is **1:1**. `lowContrastSeries` returned `[]` because it composited the background over white. A fully transparent background also returned `[]` without checking any series. Scheme detection separately uses the uncomposited RGB channels of a translucent override. Resolve the effective opaque backdrop once and use it for both L4 classification and A5 contrast. Preserve an explicit unresolved result when the backdrop cannot be determined. [color.ts:91](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/color.ts:91) · [resolve.ts:73](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/resolve.ts:73)\n\n10. **M · Reasoned — The SVG and canvas author-color inputs accept different grammars.** A value such as `url(#gradient)` is a valid SVG paint, while the canvas resolver probes it as CSS `color`, where it is invalid. A rejected SVG property update can also leave the previous series paint on a reused node because the cache records the requested value before the CSSOM accepts it. DX6 promises a series *color* consistent across renderers. Route author values through a color-valued property and use `currentColor` for SVG paint, with an explicit fallback on invalid input. The single-property CSSOM write provides no markup or extra-declaration insertion path here. [svg.ts:41](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/svg.ts:41) · [resolve.ts:95](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/resolve.ts:95)\n\n11. **M · Reasoned — Stylesheet installation can throw or leave a chart unstyled.** Without constructable or adopted stylesheets and without an active standalone sheet, `ensureStyles` unconditionally constructs, calls `replaceSync`, and spreads the adoption list. A chart inside a shadow root receives only document-level adoption, which does not style its descendants. Separately, any nonempty sentinel counts as “loaded,” and removing or disabling a detected standalone sheet never invalidates the cache. Install per rendering root, feature-detect adoption, support the standalone stylesheet fallback from plan §2.4, and verify that the expected sheet is still active. Shadow-root support is an integration assumption, not an explicit product guarantee. [styles.ts:13](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/styles.ts:13) · [css.ts:43](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:43)\n\n12. **M · Reasoned — A detached chart can resolve every paint to plausible-looking black.** A disconnected color probe can return an empty computed value. Assigning that value to a fresh canvas context leaves its initial black fill in place, which is then returned as a successful conversion. This undermines the concrete-color contract on attachment. Defer resolution until connection, or propagate an unresolved result and retry on attachment. A connected `display:none` chart is a different case because its inherited styles can still resolve. The probe batches writes, reads computed style, and removes its box on the normal path. Those reads can require style recalculation; the code does not establish a geometry layout flush per color. [resolve.ts:90](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/resolve.ts:90) · [resolve.ts:114](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/resolve.ts:114)\n\n13. **M · Reasoned — The default stylesheet’s scope defeats page-level theming in one direction and leaks in the other.** For example, `:root { --axylo-axis: red }` is masked by the default declared directly on `.axylo`. Cascade layers do let an unlayered page rule win **on the same element**, but inheritance cannot override a local declaration. Conversely, an unrelated `.axylo-text` outside a chart gets absolute positioning and disabled pointer events. The reviewed sheet also exposes no font or spacing custom properties for DX6. Use private defaults behind public token fallbacks, scope component selectors beneath `.axylo`, and wire the documented typography properties into rendering and measurement. [css.ts:15](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:15) · [css.ts:62](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:62) · [css.ts:75](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:75)\n\n14. **M · Reasoned — Overlapping bars composite differently between renderers.** Put two coincident positive rectangles in one `RectMark` with a 50%-alpha fill. Canvas fills one compound path, giving 50% coverage. SVG paints two elements, giving 75%. Coincident rectangles with opposite winding can additionally cancel in Canvas while SVG normalizes their dimensions. The same scene should produce the same image under §2.3. Choose one overlap rule, implement it in both renderers, and test an overlap pixel with an independently calculated color. [canvas.ts:202](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/canvas.ts:202) · [svg.ts:332](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/svg.ts:332)\n\n15. **m · Ran construction, reasoned redraw cost — SVG rebuilds a large `d` before discovering it is unchanged.** My 400,000-vertex path produced **3,488,890 characters** in **52 ms** in one Node run, excluding DOM parsing and painting. A draw changing only another mark still incurs this construction and string comparison. Chunking works, but the attribute cache starts too late. Let unchanged geometry skip serialization using an invalidation signal that also accounts for buffer mutation. The opt-in timing test reports samples and asserts their count; it cannot detect this regression. [svg.ts:72](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/svg.ts:72) · [svg.ts:313](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/svg.ts:313) · [timing.browser.test.ts:21](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/render/timing.browser.test.ts:21)\n\n16. **m · Ran SVG data, reasoned Canvas parity — A run with one empty area boundary can fill a triangle.** With `runs=[0,0,0,3]` and three noncollinear lower vertices, SVG emitted `M2 0L1 2L0 0Z`; Canvas closes the same polygon. The contract describes a region *between* two boundaries but leaves one-sided zero counts ambiguous. I would treat an absent side as an empty run and skip it in both implementations. Add cases for either side empty and for both empty. [svg.ts:95](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/svg.ts:95) · [canvas.ts:176](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/canvas.ts:176)\n\n17. **m · Ran layout, reasoned DOM result — Empty text lines collapse and move anchored labels.** Layout produced `[\"first\",\"\",\"last\"]` with a 54 px box at 18 px line height. The text layer creates an empty block for the middle line. With default styles it has zero height, leaving a 36 px block for the percentage translation and rotation. Give each represented line a minimum height of one computed line height, preserving user spacing. Test the rendered bounds of a middle-anchored multiline label with a blank line. [text.ts:66](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/text.ts:66) · [labels.ts:35](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/layout/labels.ts:35)\n\n18. **m · Reasoned — Several browser assertions can pass after the advertised behavior breaks.** The “all eight ... differ” test accepts five distinct ink counts and would miss swapped up/down triangles. The SVG reuse test keeps the same mark kinds and counts; it cannot detect stale children after a list changes shape or prove that unchanged attributes were never written. The A6 test proves that text grows, but never checks intersections, clipping, or relayout after a late font. Add shape-specific pixel masks, mixed-kind replacement and shrink cases, and actual bounds checks after spacing and font changes. Also exercise a non-solid **normal** compact dash for C4 and serve the text fixture under real DX8 CSP headers. [render.browser.test.ts:76](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/render/render.browser.test.ts:76) · [render.browser.test.ts:181](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/render/render.browser.test.ts:181) · [text.browser.test.ts:48](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/render/text.browser.test.ts:48)\n\n## Verification\n\nThe last lines of the four in-memory Node checks were:\n\n```text\nPASS imports, NaN lifts, area indexing/aliasing, rule edges at 4 DPRs, 400k path\nPASS opaque WCAG endpoints; low-contrast false negative reproduced\nPASS 27 text transforms against layout boxes and ordinary annular gap offsets\nPASS both opaque palettes over their specified backgrounds and four vision simulations\n```\n\n## Areas examined and found sound\n\n- **Path continuity — ran and read.** Leading, trailing, and consecutive NaN pairs lift the pen. A singleton produces a move only; the scene builder supplies its visible F2 point separately.\n- **Ordinary area runs — ran and read.** Independent vertex offsets and counts, reversed lower traversal, shared boundary arrays, and fully empty runs behaved as specified.\n- **Marker geometry — ran and read.** All seven polygon outlines wind clockwise and fit the nominal size box. Both backends use those outlines and draw circles at `size / 2`; cross and star occupy slightly less than the full box.\n- **Ordinary arcs and rules — ran.** Clockwise quarter slices preserve the specified gap at both radii. Zero span is empty and a full turn from zero is a ring. Horizontal and vertical rule edges landed on whole local device pixels at DPR 1, 1.5, 2, and 3.\n- **Canvas state and hot loops — read.** For valid marks, clip saves and restores balance, alpha and stroke dashes reset, clearing uses the identity transform, and coordinate loops allocate no object per vertex.\n- **Clipping, dashes, and overlays — read.** Only scene axis and tick rules escape the clip. Both backends honor the overlay’s two lists and clear it independently. The normal/contrast dash selection follows `DashStyle`.\n- **SVG scene reconciliation — read.** Matching slots reuse nodes, changed kinds replace them in order, and shortened lists remove trailing nodes. The overlay has its own group.\n- **Text positioning and content — ran and read.** All 27 anchor, baseline, and rotation combinations matched `PlacedText.box` for nonempty lines at matching metrics. Rendering reuses labels, writes user strings through `textContent`, and performs no layout reads between writes.\n- **Theme basics — read.** Explicit `light`, `dark`, and `only dark`, unset scheme with opaque inherited text, and an opaque background override follow L4 on initial resolution. The watcher coalesces observed changes and cleans up listeners, observer, and pending frame.\n- **Color math and palette — ran.** Comma and space RGB/RGBA, percentages, `color(srgb …)`, and `transparent` followed the expected arithmetic. Opaque black/white gave 21:1 and 50% black over white gave 3.977:1. Both default palettes passed the specified opaque-background contrast and simulated-vision distances. Raw Display-P3 and system keywords returned `null` from the pure parser; their browser normalization remains unverified."}}
